course: dictionary
lesson: 1228
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word bullet is a good example. The sentence around it tells you which meaning is right. Read the clues before you choose.
explain: A bullet can be a small piece of metal shot out of a gun, a dot in front of each item in a list, or something very fast. «The peregrine falcon is the fastest animal, diving at over three hundred kilometres an hour with its wings folded like a bullet.» Here the words are speed and diving, so bullet means very fast and straight.
explain: In school notes, «bullet points» are dots that make a list clear. In a fact file, each fact can start with a bullet point. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A bullet is a small piece of metal shot out of a gun. Guns and bullets are very dangerous, so never touch one you find. Tell an adult straight away.
fact: A bullet point is a dot (•) in front of each item in a list.
fact: «Bullet» can also mean very fast, as in «bullet train», a very fast train in Japan.
fact: «Bite the bullet» means to do something hard that you have been avoiding.
exercise: «The peregrine falcon folds its wings and drops at a pigeon like a bullet.» What does like a bullet mean here? | Very loud, with a bang | Round and soft | A small dot on a list | *Very fast and straight
exercise: Mia writes, «Use bullet points for each idea in your notes.» What is a bullet point? | *A dot in front of each item in a list | A very fast train | A piece of metal shot out of a gun | A sharp sting from an insect
exercise: «Japan's bullet train was given a kingfisher-shaped nose to make it quieter.» What is a bullet train? | *A very fast train | A small, quiet bird | A train that is shot out of a gun | A list of train times
test: You find something that looks like a real bullet on the path. What should you do? | Throw it into the nearest bin | Pick it up to look closely | Put it in your pocket to show your friends | *Do not touch it, and tell an adult
test: «To bite the bullet» means what? | Run as fast as a bullet | *Do something hard that you have been avoiding | Shoot at a target | Eat something hard and crunchy
exam: In «The bullet ant has one of the most painful insect stings known», which meaning of bullet fits best? | *Bullet ant is a name for an insect, so bullet here is part of its name | A very fast train | A small piece of metal shot out of a gun | A dot in front of a list item
